{"step_index":157,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-18T09:13:38Z","input_tokens":8023,"cache_read_tokens":326870,"output_tokens":3147,"thinking":"Investigating a potential bug related to bone rotations. The previous suspicion of a `rest-pose` axis rotation issue on a specific bone (`Bone_Heading`) now seems likely. Need to verify that the rotation assignment in pose space (`bone_heading.rotation_euler = eul`) is correct or if there is indeed a bug.\n\n\nObserved that `Bone_Heading`'s local orientation directly aligns with the world coordinate system, as indicated by the rotation assignment in V5. Initial hypothesis about axis misinterpretation now seems less likely, as the `rotation_euler.z` manipulation in V5 directly correlates to world Z-axis rotation. The rest pose matrix appears to be the identity matrix, or a rotation around X if the bone tail points along Z.\n\n\nInitial hypothesis was that a world-to-local coordinate system inversion was occurring with the Z-axis, potentially leading to incorrect pitch or bank angles. However, now considering discrepancies in calculated distances, a more fundamental error in the coordinate system definition itself is suspected, with a potential flip or inversion in the bone's local matrix. Immediate verification is required to confirm whether the local Z-axis is inverted or the pitch calculation is wrong. Further checking of the coordinate system configuration is needed to pinpoint the source of the distance errors, possibly a direct sign flip.\n\n\nBlender's coordinate system requires careful handling; initial assumptions about axis orientations proved incorrect. The cross-product calculation appears to be the core of the problem. A test script will be executed to compare the world matrices of specific bones with the road surface to identify any alignment issues. This will verify if the tires are correctly flush with the road or not.\n\n\nAnalyzing image data to identify potential exposure issues.  Specifically, `shot_21` exhibits significant underexposure, potentially due to lighting conditions and camera settings during the shot. Further investigation required for `shot_07` and `shot_24` which also seem very dark.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_file","args":{"Content":"# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-\n\"\"\"\nExact 3D Tire-to-TrackDeck Contact Check + Deep Art-Director Critique for V6 Sky-Harbor Iteration 1\n\"\"\"\nimport bpy, os, json\nfrom mathutils import Vector\n\nPROJ = r\"D:\\项目session\\blender-supercar\"\nSCRATCH = r\"C:\\Users\\86052\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\1a8ac0b5-f848-4c0e-bc45-8abba2abb2e8\\scratch\"\nbpy.ops.wm.open_mainfile(filepath=os.path.join(PROJ, \"v6_spiderverse\", \"v6_stage_anim_sv.blend\"))\nsc = bpy.context.scene\nrig = bpy.data.objects[\"RIG_F1_Race\"]\ndeck = bpy.data.objects.get(\"V6_TrackDeck\")\n\nprint(\"Bone_Root rest matrix_local:\\n\", rig.data.bones[\"Bone_Root\"].matrix_local)\nprint(\"Bone_Heading rest matrix_local:\\n\", rig.data.bones[\"Bone_Heading\"].matrix_local)\n\n# Check actual world vertices of GEO_F1_Tire_FL..RR vs closest point on V6_TrackDeck!\nfor f, label in [(1, \"StartFlat\"), (309, \"Raidillon+13.5deg\"), (635, \"Bowl+17.4degBank\"), (830, \"Corkscrew-13.9deg\"), (960, \"Tunnel341kmh\"), (1121, \"HairpinMacro\")]:\n    sc.frame_set(f)\n    dg = bpy.context.evaluated_depsgraph_get()\n    deck_e = deck.evaluated_get(dg)\n    rig_e = rig.evaluated_get(dg)\n    errs = {}\n    for wn in (\"FL\", \"FR\", \"RL\", \"RR\"):\n        tob = bpy.data.objects[f\"GEO_F1_Tire_{wn}\"].evaluated_get(dg)\n        mw = tob.matrix_world\n        # Find vertex of tire closest to V6_TrackDeck surface!\n        # Sample tire vertices in world space, project onto deck_e.closest_point_on_mesh\n        min_signed_d = 999.0\n        for v in list(tob.data.vertices)[::6]:\n            pw = mw @ v.co\n            ok, cp, norm, _ = deck_e.closest_point_on_mesh(deck_e.matrix_world.inverted() @ pw)\n            if ok:\n                cp_w = deck_e.matrix_world @ cp\n                nw = (deck_e.matrix_world.to_3x3() @ norm).normalized()\n                sd = (pw - cp_w).dot(nw)\n                if sd < min_signed_d:\n                    min_signed_d = sd\n        errs[wn] = round(min_signed_d * 1000.0, 1)  # in millimeters! (+ = floating above deck, - = penetrating deck)\n    pb_h = rig_e.pose.bones[\"Bone_Heading\"]\n    hm = rig_e.matrix_world @ pb_h.matrix\n    print(f\"Frame {f:>4} ({label:<18}): tire bottom signed clearance (mm) = {errs} | Heading Z-axis={[round(x,3) for x in hm.col[2][:3]]}\")\n\n# Also check Solidify outline thickness & ComicFX visibility at key still frames\nfor f in (81, 295, 401, 635, 1021, 1068, 1121):\n    sc.frame_set(f)\n    dg = bpy.context.evaluated_depsgraph_get()\n    active_fx = []\n    for o in bpy.data.collections[\"V6_09_ComicFX\"].all_objects:\n        oe = o.evaluated_get(dg)\n        if oe.scale.length > 0.05 and not oe.hide_render:\n            active_fx.append(f\"{o.name}(s={round(oe.scale.x,2)})\")\n    print(f\"Frame {f:>4} active ComicFX ({len(active_fx)}): {active_fx}\")\n","Overwrite":true,"Path":"C:\\Users\\86052\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\1a8ac0b5-f848-4c0e-bc45-8abba2abb2e8\\scratch\\check_v6_deep_critique.py"}},{"name":"read_board","args":{"since":39}}]}
